    // RAN: Review gate for Sprint 3 (E3a e2eeClientWiring), three passes per D0172, inspected 2026-11-10 at 1f979f6. The fixes are in the closing commit. Pass 1 was a code review of the client change by an independent reviewer: 14 findings, 1 High, 2 Medium, 11 Low. Pass 2 was a mechanism review against spec sections 4.3, 4.7, 4.8 and 4.9 by a second independent reviewer. It judged the ten DoD clauses and found 13, 2 Medium and 11 Low. Pass 3 was the author's clause-by-clause check, folded into the two lists. The High: a block in resolveCodec left the previous session's encrypted codec behind, so a manual plugin push could write under the wrong key. Fixed: every connect starts from the plain codec, and the manual push, pull, preview and remove refuse a blocked link. The Mediums, all fixed. The pin is keyed by the host-qualified vault identity. The define check scopes its match to the Decision block that owns the DependsOn edge and reads the cost from its decision field. The secrets capture boots the real plugin through the keyring arms and reads its log ring and card text. The Lows, all fixed. The join latch resets on Reconfigure. The codec cache key carries vk and clears on pin changes. fetchFileBytes needs its codec, no plain default. The lint also fails on a namespace import, a re-export, a bare identifier, a noble or streamhash import, and subtle.digest outside the allowlist. The build reads no decisions when the literal is false. The streamed pull folds the server row's path. The pin id must be canonical base64 of 16 bytes. The 503 translation covers the pair after a re-login, and the Keyring tag survives it. A pinned device with the define off syncs, pinned by a test. The real buildApi is exercised with and without a pin. The plain-codec pull test asserts the size error it meets. Named deviations: GET keyring never carries the header by design. The cursor is held under the existing retry budget, not forever. The incremental cid wraps noble's HMAC, not a streamhash digest, and the spec says so now. Scope deviation, named: of the four define-off surfaces only the unpinned 200 exists in this build, and no KDF entry exists yet. The E3b DoD now carries the rest as clauses 12 and 13. Those are the three surfaces, the three entries, the join modal, the Join action and the plugin-level secrets capture. After the fixes: client suite green, tsc clean, build clean, keel gate green. Verdict PASS.
