    // RAN: Autonomous retro for Sprint 3 (E3a e2eeClientWiring), analysed 2026-11-10. What the panel-fixed DoD got right: the connect order and the decision table of spec section 4.8. Both were exact enough to test on the real plugin. What the implementation changed: the pin key is host-qualified. The incremental cid wraps noble's HMAC. The four define-off surfaces split between E3a and E3b, and the E3b DoD now says so. Avoidable issue one: the RED codec test went into the standup commit and turned CI red on main for one commit. It is issue013 with a proposed process-change Decision, d0113, for the pre-commit guard. The script and a vitest test already exist. The convention until acceptance: the RED file stays unstaged. Avoidable issue two: a block in resolveCodec left the previous codec behind. The class is state that outlives the connect that set it. Review caught it, and a reset at the start of each connect plus a test fixed it. No new item beyond issue013. Everything else was fixed in the closing commit, and the capability's follow-ups are already tracked under d0096. Wall time: refine at 15:48, closing commit near 16:45. That is about one hour against the two-to-three-day guideline for 8 points. Verdict PASS.
